      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9c-10b &=5 \\\\ b-c &=8a\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0a-10b-9c &=5 \\\\ -8a+1b-1c &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -10 & -9 & 5 \\\\ -8 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
